.SH hee-cache-prune(1)
.PP
hee-cache-prune \[en] prune stale entries from the real hee-* disk
caches (hee-filter\[cq]s repo-visibility cache, hee-git-merge\[cq]s
PR-detail cache).
A TTL alone never deletes an entry nobody re-queries \[en] it just sits
forever.
Real trigger: Spencer\[cq]s ask, 2026-08-24, \[lq]keep things clean\[rq]
\[en] meant to be cron\[cq]d via bootstrap.mk\[cq]s own
unprivileged-by-design mechanism
(\f[V]make -f tooling/bootstrap.mk install-cron\f[R]), not a one-off
manually-copied script.
.PP
Usage: hee-cache-prune [days, default 7]
.PP
\f[I](no \[en]help/-h output \[en] generated from the script\[cq]s own
header comment)\f[R]
